WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.511 --> 00:00:17.648
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:19.417 --> 00:00:21.085
Another helicopter?

00:00:21.085 --> 00:00:24.088
I get the feeling something
doesn't want me alive.

00:00:24.088 --> 00:00:25.756
Besides the obvious.

00:00:26.524 --> 00:00:28.092
Yeah, okay.

00:00:28.092 --> 00:00:30.361
This is the wrong way.

00:00:30.361 --> 00:00:34.065
I mean, sharks, mortar shells,
attack helicopters, drowning...

00:00:34.065 --> 00:00:36.267
some force wants me dead.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.202
Maybe that's why all of
this is happening.

00:00:39.103 --> 00:00:42.073
I was SUPPOSED to die
yesterday in the test chamber

00:00:42.073 --> 00:00:44.175
but I didn't because I'm hardcore,

00:00:44.175 --> 00:00:46.644
so now reality is slowly unraveling.

00:00:46.644 --> 00:00:49.914
That makes me the most important
person in the universe.

00:00:49.914 --> 00:00:51.949
Still don't like getting shot at, though.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.951
Okay, I can jump this.

00:00:55.553 --> 00:00:57.955
[explosions]

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.092
How did this guy get here?

00:01:01.092 --> 00:01:02.927
I guess he fell out of the chopper.

00:01:02.927 --> 00:01:05.363
[explosions]

00:01:05.363 --> 00:01:08.733
Well, glad they're using up
missiles on something besides me.

00:01:08.733 --> 00:01:11.769
So, if I die, will reality
slowly correct itself

00:01:11.769 --> 00:01:13.337
or will the world just end?

00:01:14.739 --> 00:01:17.408
It might as well be the end of
the world if I'm dead!

00:01:17.408 --> 00:01:19.744
God, how many helicopters are
there?

00:01:19.744 --> 00:01:21.679
Too damned many, that's how much!

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:23.047
[explosions]

00:01:23.047 --> 00:01:25.149
Alright, yeah, more missiles.

00:01:25.149 --> 00:01:27.018
I never really had
an opinion about it before,

00:01:27.018 --> 00:01:30.388
but after today, I think we definitely
have too much military spending.

00:01:30.388 --> 00:01:31.756
That's what, 20%?

00:01:31.756 --> 00:01:33.524
It needs to be, like, 1%.

00:01:35.493 --> 00:01:36.060
Look at this guy.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.063
He's flying like he doesn't give a fuck
how many missiles he uses.

00:01:39.063 --> 00:01:40.665
He's not paying for it!

00:01:40.665 --> 00:01:43.134
He'll probably use the extras to
blow up cactuses--[missiles firing]

00:01:43.134 --> 00:01:43.768
--cacti!

00:01:43.768 --> 00:01:44.535
[explosions]

00:01:44.535 --> 00:01:46.304
YES!  FIRE MISSILES AT ME!

00:01:46.304 --> 00:01:48.406
THAT'S TOTALLY NOT OVERKILL!

00:01:48.406 --> 00:01:49.140
NO!

00:01:49.607 --> 00:01:50.775
Now, which way do I go?

00:01:50.775 --> 00:01:51.309
[helicopter firing]

00:01:51.309 --> 00:01:54.779
OH, MY GOD!  IT IS SO HARD TO
CONCENTRATE OUT HERE!

00:01:54.779 --> 00:01:56.314
Oh, nice, an arch.

00:01:56.314 --> 00:01:59.450
Yeah, let's see you shoot through
solid rock, there, tough guy.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:02.787
Man, I'm a little light on ammo
after shooting that last chopper down.

00:02:02.787 --> 00:02:05.156
I think I just got lucky on that last one.

00:02:05.156 --> 00:02:07.258
I mean, these are only, what, 9 millimeter?

00:02:07.258 --> 00:02:09.327
Their hull can probably take that.

00:02:09.327 --> 00:02:12.897
I'm pretty sure I'm not the first person
to have the idea of shooting at a helicopter.

00:02:12.897 --> 00:02:13.597
[helicopter whirring]

00:02:13.597 --> 00:02:15.232
FUUUST!  YAAAAH!

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.735
OKAY!  I NEED SOME VOLUNTEERS!

00:02:17.735 --> 00:02:20.171
WITH YOUR HELP, WE CAN SHOOT
DOWN THIS HELICOPTER!

00:02:20.171 --> 00:02:21.939
[screaming]

00:02:22.807 --> 00:02:24.942
GOD DAMMIT!
YOU'RE NOT HELPING AT ALL!

00:02:26.477 --> 00:02:28.179
DO I LOOK LIKE A HELICOPTER?!

00:02:28.179 --> 00:02:28.846
NO!

00:02:30.581 --> 00:02:32.650
I do NOT look like a helicopter!

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.219
If I did my life would be less
complicated in some ways

00:02:35.219 --> 00:02:37.088
and more complicated in others.

00:02:37.088 --> 00:02:40.091
Actually, my life's gotten
REALLY complicated lately.

00:02:40.091 --> 00:02:42.827
I guess I'm not doing
as much...math.

00:02:42.827 --> 00:02:43.995
That part's simpler.

00:02:43.995 --> 00:02:45.129
But, I like math.

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:47.665
Math has zero bullshit tolerance.

00:02:47.665 --> 00:02:49.400
"Storm drain hatch"?

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:50.101
Where?

00:02:51.202 --> 00:02:54.105
Yeah, just as I thought.
That did nothing.

00:02:54.105 --> 00:02:57.274
Storm dra-- it probably rains
here once every three years.

00:02:58.109 --> 00:02:58.943
[helicopter firing]

00:02:58.943 --> 00:03:00.745
Haaahhhhh...

00:03:00.745 --> 00:03:04.048
If I smoked, this is exactly where
I'd have a cigarette right now.

00:03:05.149 --> 00:03:06.217
Smoke tobacco.

00:03:06.217 --> 00:03:10.054
I guess I'd smoked peyote, but I'd
rather chew it or take it intravenously.

00:03:10.054 --> 00:03:11.756
Oh, here's a good hiding spot.

00:03:11.756 --> 00:03:14.125
[straining]

00:03:14.125 --> 00:03:17.328
Oh, wow.  More explosive rounds.

00:03:17.328 --> 00:03:19.864
Yeah, I could think of
a lot uses for these.

00:03:19.864 --> 00:03:23.067
Yeah, this would actually be a
terrible time to take peyote.

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:25.469
I don't see how a good trip
would be even possible.

00:03:26.437 --> 00:03:29.440
Oh, man, shells!
This is a treasure stash!

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.143
Maybe, if I'll keep looking,
I'll find a big bag of cash.

00:03:32.143 --> 00:03:34.045
That would simplify my life.

00:03:34.045 --> 00:03:37.715
Maybe since the universe is
conspiring to kill me and failing at it,

00:03:37.715 --> 00:03:40.084
that means I can break more
rules and get away with them.

00:03:40.084 --> 00:03:41.619
Like, I could go in and rob a bank,

00:03:41.619 --> 00:03:44.455
and, even though there's only
like a 30% success rate at that,

00:03:44.455 --> 00:03:45.956
I'd be the one to get away with it.

00:03:46.657 --> 00:03:47.158
[missiles firing]

00:03:47.158 --> 00:03:49.860
YAAAH!  AAAAH!  WAAAH!

00:03:51.462 --> 00:03:52.897
LEAVE ME ALONE!

00:03:52.897 --> 00:03:54.532
I'M ON MY SMOKE BREAK!

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:56.834
[straining]

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.669
[helicopter firing]

00:03:59.003 --> 00:03:59.870
Uhh....

00:04:00.638 --> 00:04:01.939
These things burrow?!

00:04:03.307 --> 00:04:04.575
I don't think so.

00:04:06.377 --> 00:04:07.545
"Mines"?!

00:04:07.545 --> 00:04:11.282
Okay... I guess don't go
passed... this... point...

00:04:11.916 --> 00:04:13.651
Fucking "Tremors" man....

00:04:13.651 --> 00:04:15.286
Oh, look, my best friend's back.

00:04:15.286 --> 00:04:18.122
Okay, time to visit Chataeu du Rock again.

00:04:18.122 --> 00:04:19.757
[straining]

00:04:19.757 --> 00:04:21.392
Don't cave in on me!

00:04:23.127 --> 00:04:26.230
Okay, I don't know what I'm looking at,

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:29.333
but, there's a dead guy, so there's that.

00:04:29.333 --> 00:04:32.036
I guess I could talk to him,
see if he knows anything.

00:04:32.036 --> 00:04:33.204
[helicopter fires]

00:04:33.204 --> 00:04:35.673
Hey, I was right.  It's
something horrible.

00:04:35.673 --> 00:04:36.841
Jesus Christ!

00:04:37.875 --> 00:04:39.977
Whoa!  Whoa!
What's the range on that thing?

00:04:40.578 --> 00:04:41.612
Wrong answer!

00:04:46.317 --> 00:04:48.018
I think I'm just pissing it off.

00:04:48.719 --> 00:04:51.255
I'll leave it alone. Maybe it'll
grab the helicopter.

00:04:51.255 --> 00:04:52.790
Then everyone will be happy.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.794
And we'll have balloons and
ice cream and cake and--

00:04:56.794 --> 00:04:58.529
Hey, I've been here already!

00:04:58.529 --> 00:05:01.065
I'd know that mound of sand anywhere!

00:05:01.065 --> 00:05:02.800
The desert tricked me!

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.369
And, God dammit,
that helicopter won't give up.

00:05:05.369 --> 00:05:06.804
I feel like all that propeller spinning

00:05:06.804 --> 00:05:09.340
should be affecting the axial
procession of the Earth,

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:10.908
even though I know it doesn't.

00:05:10.908 --> 00:05:13.978
The Coriolis Effect is not
working for me today.

00:05:13.978 --> 00:05:16.981
But, I will say that my career's turning out
much more varied than I would've thought.

00:05:16.981 --> 00:05:18.282
Nope, no treasure here.

00:05:18.282 --> 00:05:20.818
Physicists don't usually see
this kind of action.

00:05:20.818 --> 00:05:22.286
Too much action!

00:05:22.286 --> 00:05:23.087
Gyah!

00:05:23.087 --> 00:05:27.091
YAAH! YAAH! YAAH! YAAH! YAAH!

00:05:27.091 --> 00:05:27.925
Huh.

00:05:27.925 --> 00:05:31.295
This is kind of how claimed my
lab space at my first day of work.

00:05:31.295 --> 00:05:33.264
Except I didn't have a shotgun for that.

00:05:33.264 --> 00:05:34.765
But, I didn't need one.

00:05:34.765 --> 00:05:36.934
Okay, this is the wrong way;
I'll be leaving now.

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:40.638
And, I guess going in circles the other
way, maybe some options will open up

00:05:40.638 --> 00:05:41.906
even though they shouldn't, but--

00:05:41.906 --> 00:05:43.274
Okay, you are way too big.

00:05:45.809 --> 00:05:47.845
I wonder how this fits into
the ecosystem.

00:05:47.845 --> 00:05:49.947
It doesn't seem to be
actually eating anything.

00:05:51.115 --> 00:05:51.949
You missed!

00:05:52.583 --> 00:05:57.454
All right, that gives him someone new
to play with while I walk in circles again.

00:05:59.123 --> 00:06:00.491
"Mines"!

00:06:00.491 --> 00:06:01.926
Man, is he following me?

00:06:03.494 --> 00:06:04.495
[gibbering]

00:06:04.495 --> 00:06:05.062
YES!

00:06:07.765 --> 00:06:10.601
This is the place I should've
decided to take a nap.

00:06:10.601 --> 00:06:12.136
Wait for him to leave.

00:06:12.136 --> 00:06:14.538
It's too loud, though; I'm never
going to get any sleep here.

00:06:15.139 --> 00:06:16.240
So, where are these mines?

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:18.042
I guess, passed this hill?

00:06:18.042 --> 00:06:19.910
You will get--BUZZ OFF!

00:06:22.146 --> 00:06:23.981
[helicopter firing]

00:06:23.981 --> 00:06:27.151
I thought I hated mosquitoes
and then I met you.

00:06:27.151 --> 00:06:29.420
Okay, maybe he thinks
I'm going that way now.

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:32.823
You know, I think this is the first situation
I've encountered in the past two days

00:06:32.823 --> 00:06:36.327
where a grappling hook would NOT
solve all my problems.

00:06:36.327 --> 00:06:39.797
So, I guess I went in circles because I
didn't want to walk into a fucking minefield!

00:06:39.797 --> 00:06:41.265
What great options.

00:06:41.265 --> 00:06:44.268
I need a can of orange spray paint
so I can tag one of those bodies

00:06:44.268 --> 00:06:45.603
and throw it out as a decoy.

00:06:45.603 --> 00:06:46.537
[explosions]

00:06:46.537 --> 00:06:47.104
Dammit!

00:06:48.639 --> 00:06:50.441
I swear, every time I come out
from underground,

00:06:50.441 --> 00:06:52.009
you'd think the world's ending.

00:06:52.009 --> 00:06:53.344
Oh, wait, it IS ending.

00:06:53.344 --> 00:06:54.645
Because I'm alive!

00:06:54.645 --> 00:06:55.913
Whuh-haa-haa-haa!

00:06:55.913 --> 00:06:58.749
I don't think they'd put mines
on the very sides, did they?

00:06:58.749 --> 00:07:00.551
Eh, the rock wall should be good.

00:07:01.652 --> 00:07:03.554
Hell, the signs are on THIS side,

00:07:03.554 --> 00:07:06.523
so that means they're expecting
movement from the other side.

00:07:07.124 --> 00:07:08.392
Yeah, I'm good.

00:07:09.193 --> 00:07:10.928
Well, good in the Mine Department,

00:07:10.928 --> 00:07:14.498
not so good in the Helicopter-Pilot-
With-A-Hard-On-For-Me Department.

00:07:14.498 --> 00:07:17.301
Neither of these departments
were a problem before today.

00:07:17.301 --> 00:07:18.135
Hmm.

00:07:19.303 --> 00:07:21.572
Oh!  Open manhole.

00:07:21.572 --> 00:07:23.307
Okay, yeah, this'll work.

00:07:23.307 --> 00:07:28.112
It's amazing how relative deprivation in gunfire
change your attitude about things.

00:07:28.112 --> 00:07:30.414
Hm, there's barbed wire there; I guess...

00:07:31.315 --> 00:07:32.216
Jesus...

00:07:33.284 --> 00:07:34.785
[helicopter firing]

00:07:34.785 --> 00:07:38.222
Okay, I think I should just jump it,
in case there's a mine right next to it

00:07:38.222 --> 00:07:39.857
because that's something I would do.

00:07:39.857 --> 00:07:40.557
All right.

00:07:42.059 --> 00:07:44.561
A little close there.
Don't want to floss with this stuff.

00:07:45.596 --> 00:07:46.697
[explosions]

00:07:46.697 --> 00:07:49.633
Oh, my God, it's like twenty
degrees cooler down here.

00:07:50.768 --> 00:07:51.402
Oh.

00:07:51.702 --> 00:07:52.803
Of course.

00:07:53.337 --> 00:07:55.939
I'm not even surprised, I just forgot.

00:07:58.909 --> 00:08:00.567
I think there's sand in my suit.

